Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.40,0:00:08.16,C,Matcha's founding engineer page says fully remote in the US,\NCanada, Europe, the UK, Brazil and Latin America.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.41,0:00:13.77,C,But the founder's Hacker News post from October 12 says fully\Nremote, anywhere in the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.87,0:00:18.67,C,So can an engineer in India apply? One source says no. The\Nother says yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.92,0:00:24.25,C,So I built a small tool that reads a job's location text from\None or more sources.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.53,0:00:30.68,C,It returns allowed countries, time zones, EOR or contract\Nsetups, and visa sponsorship.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.79,0:00:34.86,C,When the sources disagree, it says so, with a reason, instead\Nof guessing.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.22,0:00:42.13,C,Search Atlas is the same story. Its Hacker News post says\Nanywhere. Its careers page lists six countries.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.51,0:00:48.91,C,A clear post, like PrairieLearn's, comes back as US only, no\Nvisa sponsorship, no conflict.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.03,0:00:55.85,C,I tested it on 32 real job posts with hand written labels.\NHalf were held out while I wrote the rules.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.96,0:01:03.65,C,On the held out half, the rules got every field right on 11 of\N16 jobs, and the India answer right on all 16.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.77,0:01:10.07,C,An LLM on Groq's free tier did worse, at 9 of 16. Every miss\Nis listed in the repo.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.17,0:01:13.90,C,The code, the cases, and the labels are public on GitHub.
